For every $I\in V$ and every $Y\in\overline I$, $$\label{mesh:width-bounds}
 \frac14H\bigl(\rho(Y)+\alpha\bigr)
 \le |I|\le2H\bigl(\rho(Y)+\alpha\bigr)\le2H.$$ Moreover, $|V|=2m=O(k^3\log k)$.

Let $s$ affine hyperplanes be given in $\mathbb R^e$, and record, for each hyperplane, the sign in $\{-,0,+\}$ of a defining affine function. The number of realized joint sign vectors is at most $$\label{count:arrangement-bound}
 \sum_{d=0}^e\binom{s}{d}\sum_{j=0}^{e-d}\binom{s}{j}
 \le(e+1)^2(s+1)^e.$$ The same bound applies when the parameter space is restricted to an arbitrary subset of $\mathbb R^e$.

Let $T_{\mathrm{glob}}$ be the number of words $\bigl(L(n_j)\bigr)_{0\le j<k}$ arising from the progressions in [setup:cyclic](#setup:cyclic). Then $$\label{count:global-bound}
 \log T_{\mathrm{glob}}
 =O\bigl(D(\log k+\log\lambda)\bigr)
 =O(k^{3/10}\log k)=o(M).$$

Let $\mathcal E$ be a finite family of events. Suppose a graph on $\mathcal E$, with neighbor sets $\Gamma(E)$, has the property that each $E$ is independent of the sigma-algebra generated by the events outside $\{E\}\cup\Gamma(E)$. If numbers $z_E\in(0,1)$ satisfy $$\label{outer:lll-condition}
 \mathbb P(E)\le z_E\prod_{F\in\Gamma(E)}(1-z_F)
 \qquad(E\in\mathcal E),$$ then $\mathbb P(\bigcap_{E\in\mathcal E}E^c)>0$.

Choose a heavy label and let $J$ be its set of occurrence indices, with $m_*=|J|>k/M$. Let $h$ be the smallest positive difference between two members of $J$, attained at $j'$ and $j'+h$. Set $$u=\hat x(n_{j'+h})-\hat x(n_{j'}),\qquad
 v=\tilde y(n_{j'+h})-\tilde y(n_{j'}).$$ Then, for sufficiently large $k$, $$\label{dichotomy:drift-bounds}
 \begin{gathered}
 1\le h\le2M,\\
 |u_i|\le\frac{H_x}{m_*-1}\le\frac{2MH_x}{k},\qquad
 |v_i|\le\frac{2H}{m_*-1}\le\frac{4MH}{k}
 \quad(1\le i\le D),
 \end{gathered}$$ and $v=\lambda u$ as real vectors.

With $h,u,v$ as in [dichotomy:drift](#dichotomy:drift), there is $t\in\{0,\ldots,h-1\}^D$ such that $$\label{dichotomy:path-equations}
 \begin{aligned}
 x(n_j)&=x(n_0)+\frac jh(t+u),\\
 y(n_j)&=y(n_0)+\frac jh(\lambda t+v)
 \end{aligned}
 \qquad\text{in }\mathbb T^D\quad(0\le j<k).$$ Moreover $\gcd(t_1,\ldots,t_D,h)=1$, and indices incongruent modulo $h$ have distinct full labels. Consequently, all occurrences of any one full label lie in a single residue class modulo $h$.

Let $T_{\mathrm{aff}}$ be the number of signatures realized by affine cyclic progressions, and let $T_{\mathrm{glob}}$ be the full-label word count of [count:global](#count:global). There is an absolute constant $C$ such that $$\label{perturb:signature-count}
 T_{\mathrm{aff}}
 \le C T_{\mathrm{glob}}\bigl(k(Dq^2+2)\bigr)^3.$$ In particular, $$\label{perturb:entropy}
 \log\max\{1,T_{\mathrm{aff}}\}
 \le O(k^{3/10}\log k)+6\log q+O(\log k)
 =O(k^{9/10}\log k)=o(pk).$$ All implied constants are absolute.

With integer parameters in both infima, $$\lim_{k\to\infty}
 \inf_{\substack{r\in\mathbb Z\\r\ge2}}
 \frac{\log W_r(k)}{k\log r}=\infty,
 \qquad
 \lim_{r\to\infty}
 \inf_{\substack{k\in\mathbb Z\\k\ge3}}
 \frac{\log W_r(k)}{\log r}=\infty.$$ In particular, $W_r(k)^{1/k}\to\infty$ for every fixed integer $r\ge2$, and $W_r(k)/r^A\to\infty$ as $r\to\infty$ for every fixed integer $k\ge3$ and every fixed real $A>0$.
